      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, hw quirk. Added comment and defined constant. \n\nDetails: PAC1954 requires 1 ms `t_REFRESH` after a REFRESH per the Microchip PAC194x/195x datasheet. During enabling/disabling consecutive channels on the same PAC, sleeping for 2 ms ensures each PAC finishes its REFRESH cycle before the next channel on the same PAC is configured.",
